#
# One declared rule, so an expectation naming anything else names nothing at all.
#
# Deliberately minimal. The four test data files beside this one differ only in which of the two
# conditions under test they trigger -- an expectation that ran and was not met, and an expectation
# that named a rule this file does not declare -- so anything else the rules file did would be noise
# in a test about which of the two decides the exit code.
#
rule R_ONE {
  Resources.Thing.Properties.Encrypted == true
}
